*.pdf
pdf_samples/
# 2026-08-06: broadened from `extracted_raw/*.png` to the whole directory, and added every
# other page-scan/evidence folder that was untracked but NOT covered by any rule -- one
# `git add -A` away from repeating the exposure below. All of these are copyrighted textbook
# page images or verbatim OCR text; the evidence trail is meant to stay local only.
# Glob (not one line per chapter) so a folder for a future chapter is covered automatically.
extracted_raw/
extracted_full_*/
extracted_toc/
verify_crops/
# 分卷 PDF 只保留本地（约 444 MB），说明文件仍然提交
生物化学笔记_分卷/*.pdf
node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Lehninger full-text search cache (5.7 MB of book text) - never commit
lehninger_index/_B_text.pkl
lehninger_index/_A_text.pkl
lehninger_index/dossiers/

# Offline single-file builds (tools/build-offline.py). Build artefacts, ~8 MB each;
# regenerate rather than commit.
*_offline.html

# 2026-08-15: lecture video pipeline. Source lives in lecture_pipeline/; the outputs
# do not. Subtitles and transcripts are regenerated by `stages.py cues`, the study
# app is a build artefact like *_offline.html above, and the intermediates are large.
lecture_pipeline/work/
lecture_pipeline/series/
lecture_pipeline/**/*.srt
lecture_pipeline/**/*_app.html
lecture_pipeline/**/raw_words.json
lecture_pipeline/**/cues.json
# lecture 1 predates the work/NN layout, so restore_work.py drops its two files
# at the pipeline root; the committed copies are in data/01/.
lecture_pipeline/topics.json

# 2026-08-26: the rules above were written when the intermediates lived in %TEMP%
# and were assumed regenerable. Windows then cleared %TEMP% and they were not:
# re-transcribing gives the RAW text back, while the 6142 hand-checked corrections
# exist only in cues.json. lecture_pipeline/data/ is that irreplaceable pair --
# cues.json and topics.json per lecture, ~7 MB -- plus the correction audit logs.
# It is committed on purpose. restore_work.py copies it back into place.
!lecture_pipeline/data/
!lecture_pipeline/data/**

# jiri_bank build caches. Both are regenerated by tools in that folder
# (bank_import.py and qindex.py) and _bank_raw.json alone is 3.7 MB of
# content already committed elsewhere in this repo.
jiri_bank/_bank_raw.json
jiri_bank/_qindex.json

# The Kokoro TTS weights used by tools/render-audio.py: 350 MB, Apache-2.0, and
# re-downloadable from the kokoro-onnx releases. The AUDIO it produces is committed
# (biochemie_pro/audio/) -- the model that produced it is not.
.kokoro/
# Throwaway Chrome profile the headless tools drive.
.chrome-dump-profile/
# Intermediates: regenerated by tools/dump-topics.py and tools/dump-speakables.py.
tools/topics.json
tools/speakables.json
